// #4277 drill: a routine's hold move (`h<local>@window`: a fresh key's credit
// moved into the judged set through a pooled hold local) is recorded against
// the window after the one it was moved into. A hold carries only a
// temporary's credit — a frame variable's credit moves as that variable's own
// `m` — so the set's release of the key (the key is present) is left without
// its event. Once counted as the routine's own (routine-internal), it is
// refused since #4278 B1 retired that class: the RC byte check must reject.
effect fn main() -> Unit = {
  var m: Map[String, Int] = map.from_list([("a", 1), ("b", 2)])
  m = map.set(m, string.repeat("a", 1), 3)
  println(int.to_string(map.len(m)))
}
